Workshop revision: final 90-minute programme
============================================

Base commit:  8b88f32 docs(site): refresh the rendered workshop
Branch:       chore/claude-code-setup (uncommitted working tree)
Created:      2026-11-21
Size:         27 files changed, 1970 insertions(+), 1138 deletions(-)

To apply it from a clean checkout of the base commit, run:

    git apply --index workshop-revision.diff

git apply ignores everything above the first "diff --git" line. Renames are
written as the git mv pairs used in the revision, not as git's similarity
guesses. The published site in docs/ is not refreshed or included.


Summary
=======

The workshop now follows the final 90-minute programme: 42 minutes of concepts
and demonstrations, 40 minutes of hands-on exercises and 8 minutes of
discussion. Each segment has its own lesson. The revision is built on three
foundations:

  - One dataset throughout: HealthWellbeing (Harrer et al., section 4.2.4).
    vetiver uses a small supplementary lm() model, because the meta-analysis
    model is not supported by its standard interface.
  - One continuous hands-on exercise: participants complete a partially
    finished targets pipeline and Quarto report, copied to an ignored
    workspace/ folder, then modify the analysis and reproduce the results.
  - One prepared environment: MyBinder, with no installation during the
    session. The dataset versions are prepared before the session.

The main learning outcome is to understand and experience an end-to-end
reproducible research workflow, not to master each package.


